Known issues in OceanDirect
1. General (all spectrometers)
  a. getIndicesAtWavelengthRange – Always returns a small value (Ex: 2E-315) as the value for the last wavelength. This is incorrect.
  b. isFeatureEnabled enums are mis-numbered when accessed in Matlab. This does not affect queries in C#.

2. OFX/HDX
  a. getBoxcarWidth and setBoxcarWidth are not valid for this spectrometer. They return errorCode = 6 instead of the correct errorCode = 5 or 24.
  b. All commands regarding DC Input and Output on GPIO pins are under development and have not been fully tested.
    i. getVoltageDCInputVolts 
    ii. getNumberOfVoltageDCOutputs
    iii. getMaximumOutputVoltageDC
    iv. getMinimumOutputVoltageDC
    v. configureAltPin (AnalogOut)
    vi. setVoltageDCOutVolts
  c. Ipv4Controller() functions work but only with DHCPEnabled set to true, ie. only dynamically granted IP addresses are valid.      setStaticIpAddress, deleteStaticIpAddress do not work.

3. QEPro
  a. Spectral_Processing Advanced Feature returns false but the feature under it applicable to the QEPro – external trigger  - works as expected.
  b. Optical Bench queries produce errorCode = 6 instead of the correct errorCode = 5 or 24.

4. Flame
  a. Spectral_Processing Advanced Feature returns false but the feature under it applicable to the Flame – external trigger  - should be true.
  b. The external trigger functions do not work as expected. 

5. STS 2.0
  a. lampEnable does not enable/disable the output pin. The errorCode returned is 0 but the electrical signal does not change.
  b. setStrobeEnable(SingleStrobe) does not work but the errorCode returned is 0.
  c. getStrobeMaximumWidth(SingleStrobe) always returns 0 with an errorCode = 0.
  d. Optical Bench queries, getSlitWidth, setSerialNumber(OpticalBench) produce errorCode = 6 and no valid value.

6. Matlab and Labview program will crash the seconds time the programs runs. For some reason, it works well on the first run but
   always crash the second time.